 1| //! The issue triage job: read, ask, decide.
 2| //!
 3| //! Read-only by construction. This module takes a [`ForgeRead`] and can no more
 4| //! post a comment than a lane can — [`crate::issues::apply`] does that, later,
 5| //! from the plan this returns. That is the same split `src/app/review.rs` makes
 6| //! and for the same reason.
 7| //!
 8| //! The order of operations is the security property. Candidates are chosen
 9| //! deterministically *before* the model is asked; the model picks from that
10| //! list; the number it picks is re-fetched from the forge; and only then does
11| //! the pure gate in [`crate::issues::close`] decide. A model that answers
12| //! "close everything" changes nothing, because the only thing it can influence
13| //! is which of a handful of real numbers is offered as evidence.
